{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/10231-mythological-corporate-environment","id":10231,"title":"Mythological corporate environment","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-13T23:01:16-08:00","id":10231,"title":"Mythological corporate environment","content":"I'm running a scion game where the characters are getting mildly getting somewhat involved with a corporation. They're all on payroll and being kept on retainer to deal with the divine. I'm mostly using this for their hero stage while they get wrapped up in bigger things.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, I've recently been thinking about how to make what is (in most ways) a normal corporation something mythical.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining things like an office nymph-alike named Mr. Tweed who survives in middle management and drowns others like a naiad in corporate policies and busywork. Alternatively Ms. Tweed would be an attractive executive assistant who wears just enough to meet dress code, speaks in a flirtatious manner, wields the power of her boss, and will drown an unsuspecting fool who takes the bait in overcommitment and/or sexual harassment charges. Mr. Tweed was my original idea, but gradually transformed into Ms. Tweed as a result of my brain pointing out that nymphs trend toward the female. Alternative, I might use both and make them the same person based on the idea that Tweed can be whatever your heart desires...in an employee.<br /> <br /> What other cool ways might one make the officeplace mythological? I'm looking for ideas from outdated to cutting edge. Mythological beings trying to cope with thing like women in the workplace or computers doing all the work can be just as fun as the IT guy extracting actual gremlins from a PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b> Onyx Path Forum Moderator</b></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Read the rules</a><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">This is my mod voice.</span></b><br /> This is not my mod voice.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9-sparketh","name":"Sparketh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T02:11:39-08:00","id":10279,"title":"","content":"Having a office building with a social hierarchy that reflects the job status hierachy. The ruling directors on the top and the humble janitors in the basement. What a few exceptions like the troll-like cleaning lady that guards her domain between the cubicles in the night, the flee into a cave apartment in the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/854-light-hero","name":"light-hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T02:32:55-08:00","id":10284,"title":"","content":"How about taking the idea of taking people in a corporation that control access to a particular area being analogous to mythical guardian creatures? So, you have the three IT guys who jealously guard access to the company servers in the basement of the building and who you can only get past by lulling with sugary treats or with metal/electronica music. Perhaps they only normally let corporate drone types past, because they're sure these 'walking dead' won't do anything to disrupt their precious systems,<br /> <br /> How you work Cerberus or Kerberos into their names is up to you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/630-vidiian","name":"Vidiian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T03:38:33-08:00","id":10300,"title":"","content":"If you want to mix and match mythologies, then you could have the HR person be a judge of Ma'at. If you are found wanting, then you will be punished by many hours of long boring seminars and workshops that drain your will and seek to break your spirit. But, if you are judged worthy, then your office is plush and on the corner and very high up with it's own private bathroom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T08:32:26-08:00","id":10430,"title":"","content":"Or Mr. Minos could be the head of HR, if you're sticking with the Greeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T08:50:33-08:00","id":10446,"title":"","content":"With the mail room in the basement, the job of office mail boy starts to look a lot like Sisyphus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Need some online tools, including a Scion/Exalted battle wheel? <a href=\"http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">http://rpg-tools.org/generators/index.php</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/829-james-mcmurray","name":"James McMurray","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T09:06:38-08:00","id":10467,"title":"","content":"And every day, he has to start delivering the mail at the bottom of the building, dropping off and picking up mail as he goes along. At the end of the day, he has to drop everything he picked up down a mail chute. The catch is, they only ever have INTERNAL mail and packages. So, tomorrow, the same stuff he just picked up, he has to deliver and pick up the stuff he dropped off the day before.<br /> <br /> An endless cycle of mail delivery.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T10:12:59-08:00","id":10528,"title":"","content":"Hermes has taken a job as a delivery boy for those few things that do go outside the office, and he couldn't be happier. Nobody ever knows where he is or what he's doing, but he leaves every morning with a bag full of stuff and it always gets where it's supposed to go. He will never answer his cellphone or log his destinations, but he's always got the signatures to prove they went where they should.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T14:30:31-08:00","id":10780,"title":"","content":"These are all great guys. My initial idea may have been Greek, but I am trying to come up with non-Greek as well.<br /> <br /> I especially like the Ma'at-like HR person. I forsee a resume-scale.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b> Onyx Path Forum Moderator</b></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Read the rules</a><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">This is my mod voice.</span></b><br /> This is not my mod voice.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9-sparketh","name":"Sparketh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T17:17:01-08:00","id":10924,"title":"","content":"There is a tree in the atrium. In order to fully understand corporate procedures, all new employees must undergo a 9-hour seminar at the base of the tree.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T17:46:45-08:00","id":10940,"title":"","content":"Everyone in engineering is short, thick, bearded, and obsessed with metallic objects. Not substantially different from any other engineering department, but these guys are mythical dwarves.<br /> <br /> There's one executive everyone knows. He's charming and he has a lot of influence at his disposal, and he's quite competent at making sure projects succeed. He wears mirrored sunglasses constantly (sensitive eyes, he says. There's a doctor's note) and is constantly seen either smoking or in a haze of smoke as if he'd recently partook. He drives a brand new black Jaguar (brand new every single year it seems). Every year, he picks some new employee and mentors him, (it's always a him), teaching him, until the young man is basically doing the exec's job... then, once the year is up, the young man seems to disappear. Reasons differ for years gone by. Better offer at another company. Family issues. Got married to someone living across the country. Car accident. There's always documentation left, but no one ever sees him again. And no one seems to find it odd as the cycle starts anew.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/267-griffinguy24","name":"griffinguy24","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar267_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T20:28:45-08:00","id":11025,"title":"","content":"You can always name the three most important server clusters down in the basement Clotho Lachesis and Atropos","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Games are a way for us to explore what it means to be human, or inhuman, as the case may be. Let's all have a good time playing them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/400-guitarsniper","name":"guitarsniper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T21:15:21-08:00","id":11046,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... I guess it depends on how &quot;modern&quot; you want things to get. The OSI (Occult Scene Investigation) series by Jes Battis is a bit &quot;adult&quot; at times considering the author is a some kinda sociology professor that focuses on alternate sexual behavior, but it has a really interesting way of blending magic, office politics and forensic police work that you might find useful. The Dresden Files has Monoc Securities which is a Norse-based company that hires out Einherjar and Valkyries as highly paid &quot;security consultants&quot;. The CEO has one eye and two black-haired secretaries. You might even look at the evil law firm from Angel, Wolfram &amp; Hart, for some ideas on blending the supernatural with bureaucracy. <br /> <br /> Just for simple stuff, maybe they make office presentations in glowing magical runes instead of on PowerPoint slides. They don't have paperwork, they have giant stacks of clay tablets to sort through. How crazy are you aiming for, and how much of a sense of humor is involved?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-14T23:23:35-08:00","id":11085,"title":"","content":"The Dresden Files has done something very similiar with the Monc Securities. Without serious spoilers: It's CEO, Donar Vadderung is an old, white-bearded rogue with one eye. His two receptionists seem like attractive women, but are pretty menacing. And vaguely birdlike, with inhuman traits like fingernails that can cut steel. And go by &quot;H&quot; and &quot;M&quot;. The building is a skyscraper of with a seemingly infinite number of floors, filled with weapons and soldiers. Mercenaries who are very skilled, and sometimes referred to as Einherjar. Sometimes, ones who've been killed while on jobs can be spotted reassuming their place in the building until the next contract. Higher level operatives tend to have superhuman attributes and are extremely knowledgeable about the occult and ancient magic, and at least one is a Valkyrie. Interestingly, the technology used is at least several generations ahead of the best stuff in use in the mortal world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/938-bigbad","name":"BigBad","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T12:00:10-08:00","id":12207,"title":"","content":"If I ever did this for myself, I think I would have the major deities stepping into minor corporate roles. After thousands of years of running the universe, they are tired and really have no patience for corporate ways. Instead they go for the jobs with less responsibility and more freedom to do as they please. Hence the example of Hermes I posted above.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":375,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","user":"Papa Bear","date":". 11-16-2013, 03:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-16T16:11:03-08:00","id":12350,"title":"","content":"What I'm ultimately going for is exploring how the supernatural has slipped into a corporate environment more than a supernatural corporation. Yes, this is an organization run by a more relatable titan (similar to Prometheus), but some mythical things that thrive in this environment will not be things he has put into place. Some things, his hired Scions might need to deal with.<br /> <br /> That being said, everything above is pretty awesome whether or not it applies to my game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b> Onyx Path Forum Moderator</b></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Read the rules</a><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#B22222\">This is my mod voice.</span></b><br /> This is not my mod voice.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9-sparketh","name":"Sparketh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T17:19:24-07:00","id":92549,"title":"","content":"I actually had something similar in a game I ran a long time ago. It was a fairly normal research and development corporation with the exception of the mysterious CEO. To start with the corporation hired the band separately for a investigation that need their various &quot;specialties&quot; . After meeting the CEO Arty Fowl he sends them globe trotting as a band gathering various artifacts to help the war against the Titans. After a very long time they discover that Arty was actually a scion of Loki who died on a mission from his father in a cave in the deserts outside of Vegas. It then got even more complected when they realize it is still the real Arty except its only his ghost given a semblance of life by one of the Titans. Oh and his ghost is tied to his skull which is now a crazy weird relic that keeps him alive. Not really what you were looking for but I hope it might have given you some ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Every normal man must be tempted at times to spit upon his hands, hoist the black flag, and begin slitting throats.&quot;<br /> -H.L. Mencken","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2486-irisheathen","name":"Irisheathen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2486_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-16T22:09:55-07:00","id":92652,"title":"","content":"Well, in the game I'm currently playing I'm planning to have my scion of Loki use his savings as a high-stakes gambler start up one of those ubiquitous/incredibly annoying asset management/office efficiency consulting firms, and use it as a front for scamming corporations and venture capitalism...you know, equal parts Bernie Madoff and the Bobs from <i>Office Space</i>.<br /> <br /> Mostly because my ST already told me I wasn't allowed to use Chaos and Magic to crash the stock market again. Or set maenads <i>also </i>hopped up on jotunblut loose in the NYSE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 03-17-2014, 01:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}